  "slug": "biological-brain-types-006a",
  "summary": "Untargeted metabolomics annotation is moving beyond whole-spectrum similarity toward fragment-level anchors and learned spectrum-to-function mapping.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is extracting biological meaning from tandem mass spectra in untargeted metabolomics. ANCHor moves annotation beyond whole-spectrum similarity by using fragment anchors shared among similar spectra, and it is applied to untargeted metabolomics features. Spec2Function takes a complementary route, inferring biological functions directly from MS2 spectra with a dual-encoder contrastive model and retrieval-augmented generation. What is new is the coupling of contrastive spectrum representations with retrieval-augmented generation to link spectra to function, rather than to structural identity alone. SynCED, a published update of the Toxin and Toxin Target Database, is a reference resource for synthetic chemical exposure data. It is heterogeneous relative to the two preprints and is included as a database rather than as a modelling advance.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
